 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Part of the standalone hydration thermodynamic cycle for acetaldehyde:        
 INPUT CARD>!   dG_hydration = G(hydrate) - [G(aldehyde) + G(water)]                        
 INPUT CARD>! -- the direct analogue of the chloroacetaldehyde caa008 series, and the       
 INPUT CARD>! genuine calibration case: Sorensen & Jencks (JACS 1987, 109, 4675)            
 INPUT CARD>! report the experimental hydration equilibrium constant for acetaldehyde       
 INPUT CARD>! directly, K_h = 1.2 +/- 0.1 at 25 C, I = 1.0, corresponding to                
 INPUT CARD>! dG_experimental = -RT ln(K_h) = -0.11 kcal/mol (54.5% hydrate, 45.5%          
 INPUT CARD>! aldehyde -- essentially thermoneutral, a sensitive test case).                
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Kept at the SAME level of theory as the rest of the aa001 series              
 INPUT CARD>! (wB97X-D/6-21G+(d,p)/PCM(water), i.e. GBASIS=N21 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1            
 INPUT CARD>! NPFUNC=1 DIFFSP=.t.) rather than switching basis mid-project, unlike          
 INPUT CARD>! the earlier chloroacetaldehyde work.                                          
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! Starting geometry: extracted from the converged aa001h structure (the         
 INPUT CARD>! IRC endpoint confirmed via bond-length analysis to be the genuine             
 INPUT CARD>! aldehyde -- C3=O4 = 1.255 A, a genuine double bond, both spectator            
 INPUT CARD>! waters unbonded to C3), taking just the 7 atoms belonging to the              
 INPUT CARD>! aldehyde itself and discarding both spectator waters. NZVAR=15                
 INPUT CARD>! (3*7-6) for this smaller, 7-atom system. No $ZMAT NONVDW exclusions           
 INPUT CARD>! needed here (those were specifically for managing artificially-close          
 INPUT CARD>! inter-fragment H-bond contacts within the larger cluster).                    
